# cron-runner scheduler crontab — real crond syntax. Each line runs the bundled
# dispatcher, which triggers one GitHub Actions workflow via the REST API.
#
#   m h dom mon dow  /scheduler/dispatch.sh  TYPE  OWNER/REPO  WORKFLOW  REF
#
# TYPE is `workflow` (a file in .github/workflows/). Example lines:
#
#   */10 * * * *  /scheduler/dispatch.sh  workflow  owner/repo  update.yml   main
#   0 3 * * *     /scheduler/dispatch.sh  workflow  owner/repo  nightly.yml  develop
#
# Lines starting with # are ignored. No shell commands — dispatch.sh only
# triggers GitHub Actions workflows.
#
# PaaS/Dokploy alternative: instead of this file, set the CRONTAB env var with
# pipe-separated entries:
#   CRONTAB=*/10 * * * * /scheduler/dispatch.sh workflow owner/repo update.yml main
*/10 * * * * /scheduler/dispatch.sh workflow owner/repo update.yml main